  <!-- Detailed Policy Sections -->
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-sm space-y-8 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">

    <!-- Section 1 -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950 tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-100 pb-2">
        <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-slate-900 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-mono">1</span>
        HTTP Cache Headers & Static Asset Optimization
      </h2>
      <p>
        To deliver instantaneous response times across web and mobile browsers, TrueLabel applies differentiated caching rules depending on data volatility:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
        <li><strong>Static Assets (CSS, Fonts, Logos, Client JS)</strong>: Served with long-lived immutable cache directives (<code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">max-age=31536000, immutable</code>) via reverse proxy. Assets are revision-stamped on deployment.</li>
        <li><strong>Public Catalog Views & Product Details</strong>: Cached with short-lived revalidation headers to maintain performance while guaranteeing freshness.</li>
        <li><strong>Authenticated Health Profiles & Personal Intake</strong>: Enforced with <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate</code> to prevent local shared workstation caches from exposing personal allergen conditions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2 -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950 tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-100 pb-2">
        <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-slate-900 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-mono">2</span>
        Real-Time Cache Invalidation Protocols
      </h2>
      <p>
        In food safety architecture, stale cached data can endanger consumer health. TrueLabel adheres to strict invalidation hooks:
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-2 pt-1">
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs">
          <strong class="text-slate-900">Event A · Manufacturer Product Update:</strong> When a food manufacturer updates an ingredient list or dietary tag, cached catalog search items and detail views are immediately flushed.
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs">
          <strong class="text-slate-900">Event B · Inspector Accreditation Decision:</strong> When an inspector approves or rejects a compliance document, the public verification registry updates instantaneously.
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs">
          <strong class="text-slate-900">Event C · Consumer Preference Change:</strong> Modifying saved allergies immediately updates the conflict detection state across all catalog products on the user's active session.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3 -->
